            "text": "{\n  \"judgments\": [\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0000\",\n      \"source_refs\": [\n        \"F005\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"In § 91.107(a)(3), the rule states that during surface movement for seaplane and float-equipped rotorcraft operations, the person pushing off or mooring the craft is excepted from the preceding seating and safety belt requirements. Connecting exemption C0003 to baseline requirement C0002 with an exception relation is directly supported by the text.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"supported\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0001\",\n      \"source_refs\": [\n        \"F003:F005\",\n        \"F024\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Section 91.107(b) establishes that, unless otherwise stated, the section does not apply to operations conducted under part 121, 125, or 135. Connecting this exemption (C0015) to the primary duties of the section in paragraph (a)—represented by C0000, C0001, and C0002—with an exception relation faithfully models the statutory scope.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"supported\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0002\",\n      \"source_refs\": [\n        \"F005\",\n        \"F024\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Section 91.107(b) expressly provides that paragraph (a)(3) does not apply to persons subject to § 91.105. Connecting exemption C0016 to baseline requirement C0002 (which captures paragraph (a)(3)) via an exception relationship accurately reflects the text.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"supported\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
